{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/i5w1os","slide":2,"text":"The critical failure point is the receiver. Ronin, Wormhole, and Nomad differ in incident details, but each illustrates the danger of a cross-chain message reaching a contract that can execute it. Portcullis adds an independent pre-transfer decision at that boundary.\n\nSource: project threat model supplied with the deck and README.md."}
