{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/x97akf","slide":3,"text":"The adapter calls the guard before transfer. The guard evaluates binding, bounds, replay, nonce, rate, and volume or policy. A plain invalid message is rejected without changing receiver state. Only an authenticated rate breach, volume spike, or explicit policy denial can latch the circuit breaker.\n\nSource: contracts/core/PortcullisChecks.sol and docs/security-notes.md."}
